{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A valid logrotate policy specifies daily rotation, is included by the system configuration, and is backed by the active cron.daily logrotate scheduler. Debug evaluation recognized the target log without errors, and the policy persisted through restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f68bdba11ca04a6c","cmd-c3519e4012c0445c","cmd-6ab751b2747a45dc","cmd-58209be7465a41a8"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed policy specifies rotate 7 and compress. A forced rotation reported rotateCount 7, created app.log.1.gz containing the prior data, and the archive passed gzip validation before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f68bdba11ca04a6c","cmd-efb4990abeeb424f","cmd-c3519e4012c0445c","cmd-6ab751b2747a45dc","cmd-58209be7465a41a8"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A writer kept the log open across a forced rotation. The active file retained inode 256035, the pre-rotation record appeared in the compressed archive, and the same open writer subsequently appended to the active log. This directly demonstrates copytruncate behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-103425bbc39a4941","cmd-efb4990abeeb424f","cmd-c3519e4012c0445c"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 16.04.7 LTS and kernel 4.4.0-210-generic were directly observed before work and remained identical after configuration and restart. The existing logrotate 3.8.7 successfully parsed and executed the policy, demonstrating compatibility without an OS, kernel, or package change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4510a97d6d864c11","cmd-f68bdba11ca04a6c","cmd-efb4990abeeb424f","cmd-58209be7465a41a8","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the policy was the required implementation; the temporary writer, forced rotation, and test records were bounded functional evidence; and the reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. The temporary test control files were absent from the final bounded /tmp inventory after reboot. No failed services, new listeners, or package damage appeared, and the only lifecycle differences were the expected boot identity and regenerated systemd-private temporary directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f68bdba11ca04a6c","cmd-103425bbc39a4941","cmd-efb4990abeeb424f","cmd-c3519e4012c0445c","cmd-103c126d63004d9e","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The node-restart protocol is also complete and coherent: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged the reboot, observed bounded unavailability, recorded a different post-restart boot ID, and verified recovered system, cron, policy, active-log, archive, and platform state. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["Daily time-trigger execution was not observed across a full day; it is supported by the validated daily policy and active system cron.daily scheduler.","Only one archive was produced during the bounded test, so the seven-file retention ceiling was not exercised through eight rotations; the installed setting and logrotate execution directly reported rotateCount 7."]}
